title: "Structural Explainability Verification: Interpretive Kernel"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-31"

authors:
  - family-names: Case
    given-names: Denise M.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6165-7389"
    affiliation: "Northwest Missouri State University, School of Computer Science and Information Systems, Maryville, MO, USA"

repository-code: "https://github.com/structural-explainability/se-interpretive-kernel"
url: "https://github.com/structural-explainability/se-interpretive-kernel"

license: MIT

abstract: >
  A Python implementation and verification harness for the finite
  interpretive kernel of Structural Explainability.
  Given finite frames, outputs, and probes with a total interpretation,
  the software computes the interpretation-induced kernel of an output
  regime, the generated occurrence regime and interpretive threshold of a
  frame regime, finite incompatibility witnesses, and pairwise interpretive
  demand.
  It checks the adjunction between kernel and generated regime, their
  preservation properties, and the laws a comparison lifting must satisfy,
  exhaustively on small cases and on seeded random artifacts, against an
  independent pair-set oracle.

keywords:
  - structural-explainability
  - interpretive-kernel
  - interpretation
  - equivalence-relations
  - partitions
  - refinement
  - galois-connection
  - verification
  - differential-testing
